#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "There are two support collection methods, the first utilizes the legacy flow-tools binaries and the second leverages Cacti's own PHP based flow stream server."
msgstr "Kuna mbinu mbili za ukusanyaji zinazotumika, ya kwanza hutumia faili tumizi za zamani za flow-tools na ya pili hutumia seva ya mtiririko wa data ya Cacti yenyewe inayotegemea PHP."

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "Bind to address"
msgstr "Fungamanisha na anwani"

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "If Cacti server has more IP Addresses, you can specify specific interface. Leave as 0.0.0.0 for primary interface."
msgstr "Ikiwa seva ya Cacti ina Anwani nyingi za IP, unaweza kubainisha kiolesura mahususi. Acha kama 0.0.0.0 kwa kiolesura kikuu."

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "Allowed Host Range"
msgstr "Masafa ya Kipangishi Yanayoruhusiwa"

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "IP Address of the device that is allowed to send to this flow collector.  Leave as 0.0.0.0 for any host.  Note that PHP is finicky about what it allows.  CIDR syntax is supported as well as range syntax for example 192.168.1.0 or 192.168.1.0/24.  If you want specific IP addresses, separate them by a comma."
msgstr "Anwani ya IP ya kifaa kinachoruhusiwa kutuma kwa kikusanyaji hiki cha mtiririko.  Acha kama 0.0.0.0 kwa kipangishi chochote.  Kumbuka kuwa PHP ina masharti makali kuhusu inachoruhusu.  Muundo wa CIDR unatumika pamoja na muundo wa masafa kwa mfano 192.168.1.0 au 192.168.1.0/24.  Ikiwa unataka anwani mahususi za IP, zitenganishe kwa mkato."

